#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bernoulli_b

#% text
# `bernoulli_b(n)` gives the Bernoulli number `B_n`; `bernoulli_b(n, x)` gives the Bernoulli polynomial.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `B_1` is `-1/2`; odd indices above 1 give 0. The numbers are exact rationals from the tangent number recurrence of Brent and Harvey, so `bernoulli_b(1000)` takes a moment but is exact.

#% item
# `bernoulli_b(n, x)` is the polynomial `sum(binomial(n, k) B_k x^(n - k))`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bernoulli_b(12)
#% output
#= -691/2730

#% cell
bernoulli_b([0, 1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= [1, -1/2, 1/6, 0, -1/30]

#% cell
bernoulli_b(3, x)
#% output
#= (1/2)*x - (3/2)*x^2 + x^3

#% cell
denominator(bernoulli_b(100))
#% output
#= 33330

